---
id: org.dxos.plugin.agent
name: AgentPlugin
version: 0.1.0
---

Manages autonomous agents in a space: assistant `Agent` objects that converse with
people from Discord threads and Composer chats, interview them, and keep what they learn as ECHO
objects — `Memory` claims and `Goal`s linked to the `Person` or `Organization` they are about.

This document records what is built. Design intent lives in [`docs/DESIGN.md`](./docs/DESIGN.md)
(architecture, EDGE gateway, identity) and [`docs/MEMORY.md`](./docs/MEMORY.md) (the memory graph and
the interview skill); items there that are not built are listed under "Not built" below rather than
specified.

The plugin depends on `org.dxos.plugin.assistant` (which registers `Agent`, `Chat` and `HasSubject`
and renders the Agent article). It ships a workerd variant with no React surfaces and no Discord
operations, so EDGE's operation service can host the agent and memory operations.

## Extensions

The following extension dialects are used in this document. `op@1.1`, `test@1.0` and `step@1.0`
are defined in [`packages/reflect/deus/lang/qa.mdl`](../../reflect/deus/lang/qa.mdl); `node`,
`companion` and `surface` in [`packages/reflect/deus/lang/app.mdl`](../../reflect/deus/lang/app.mdl); `skill@1.0` in
[`packages/plugins/plugin-crm/PLUGIN.mdl`](../plugin-crm/PLUGIN.mdl); the rest in the Appendix.

| Term        | URI                            |
|-------------|--------------------------------|
| `type`      | `org.dxos.mdl.type@1.0`        |
| `feat`      | `org.dxos.mdl.feat@1.0`        |
| `scenario`  | `org.dxos.mdl.scenario@1.0`    |
| `component` | `org.dxos.mdl.component@1.0`   |
| `op`        | `org.dxos.mdl.op@1.1`          |
| `skill`     | `org.dxos.mdl.skill@1.0`       |
| `node`      | `org.dxos.mdl.node@1.0`        |
| `companion` | `org.dxos.mdl.companion@1.0`   |
| `surface`   | `org.dxos.mdl.surface@1.0`     |
| `test`      | `org.dxos.mdl.test@1.0`        |
| `step`      | `org.dxos.mdl.step@1.0`        |

## External types

Used, not defined, here: `Agent` and `Chat` (`@dxos/assistant`), `Instructions` and `Skill`
(`@dxos/compute`), `Feed` (`@dxos/echo`), `AccessToken` (`@dxos/link`), `Person`, `Organization` and
the `HasSubject` relation (`@dxos/types`), `ProfileOf` (`@dxos/plugin-crm`, registered here too so
profiles can be written without plugin-crm enabled) and `Markdown.Document` (`@dxos/plugin-markdown`).

## Types

```mdl
type DiscordBinding
  desc: |
    Binds an agent to a Discord bot. Typename `org.dxos.type.agent.discordBinding@0.1.0`.
    Parented to its agent (`Obj.Parent`), so it is deleted with the agent; at most one per agent is
    expected and `loadForAgent` returns the first child binding. Label: `applicationId`.
  fields:
    agent: Ref<Agent>               # hidden from forms; set once by make()
    accessToken: Ref<AccessToken>   # "Bot token"
    applicationId: string           # "Application ID"; also the EDGE route key
    guildId?: string                # "Server ID"
    channels: string[]              # Discord channel ids the bot listens in
```

```mdl
type DiscordBinding.Properties
  desc: The user-editable subset of DiscordBinding (everything but `agent`); the binding form's schema.
  fields:
    accessToken: Ref<AccessToken>
    applicationId: string
    guildId?: string
    channels: string[]
```

```mdl
type GatewayState
  literals: idle | connecting | ready | closed | failed
```

```mdl
type BotStatus
  desc: Mirrors the EDGE compute-service `DiscordBotStatus`; every bot route answers with one.
  fields:
    running: boolean
    gateway: GatewayState
    config?: { spaceId: string, agent: string, applicationId: string, accessTokenId: string, channels: string[], binding?: string }
    botUserId?: string
    threads: number                 # Discord threads mapped to chats
    lastError?: string              # why the gateway last failed; EDGE retries on a watchdog
```

```mdl
type Memory
  desc: |
    One atomic, third-person claim about one or more entities. Typename
    `org.dxos.type.agent.memory@0.1.0`. Linked to each subject by a `HasSubject` relation
    (source = memory, target = entity). Never overwritten: a contradiction supersedes. Label: `content`.
  fields:
    content: string
    kind: fact | preference | goal | commitment | relationship | event
    origin: stated | inferred       # default stated
    confidence?: number             # 0..1, checked by recordMemory
    observedAt: DateTime            # default now
    status: active | superseded | retracted   # default active
    supersedes?: Ref<Obj>           # the memory this one replaces
    source?: Ref<Obj>               # the message or chat it came from (optional as built)
```

```mdl
type Goal
  desc: |
    A goal held by one or more people or organizations. Typename
    `org.dxos.type.agent.goal@0.1.0`. New goals are `proposed`; only the owner's confirmation
    moves them on. `owners` cannot be typed as Person | Organization in the schema, so the operations
    enforce it. Label: `title`.
  fields:
    title: string
    description?: string
    horizon: now | quarter | year | long-term
    status: proposed | confirmed | active | achieved | dropped
    owners: Ref<Obj>[]              # Person | Organization, checked by suggestGoal
    parent?: Ref<Obj>               # the goal this one serves
```

```mdl
type Profile
  desc: |
    Not a stored type — a `Markdown.Document` parented to the subject and linked to it by `ProfileOf`,
    rendered deterministically by `Profile.render` from the subject's live goals (sections Goals,
    Proposed goals, Achieved goals; dropped omitted) and active memories grouped by kind (Facts,
    Preferences, Aspirations, Commitments, Relationships, Events; inferred ones marked _(inferred)_).
    Regenerated, never edited as the source of truth.
```

## Operations

Agent operations (`AgentOperationHandlerSet`, every host including workerd).

```mdl
op createAgent
  key: org.dxos.operation.agent.create
  desc: Creates an autonomous agent with its instructions, first chat and context bindings.
  input:
    name: string
    instructions?: string           # markdown; default ''
  output: { agent: Ref<Agent> }
  effects: [echo:write]
  requires: [Database.Service]
  note: |
    `Agent.makeInitialized` with the Interview skill in the agent's Instructions skill set and the
    Agent conversation skill bound to the first chat. The Agents section's + action invokes it with name ''.
```

```mdl
op ensureThreadChat
  key: org.dxos.operation.agent.ensureThreadChat
  desc: Returns the chat mirroring a Discord thread for the agent, creating it on first contact.
  input:
    agent: Ref<Agent>
    threadId: string
    title?: string                  # names a new chat
    channelId?: string
  output: { chat: Ref<Chat>, feed: Ref<Feed> }
  effects: [echo:read, echo:write]
  requires: [Database.Service]
  note: |
    Idempotent on (agent, threadId): the chat carries `Obj.Meta` keys `{ source: 'discord.com', id:
    threadId }` and, when given, `{ source: 'discord.com/channel', id: channelId }`; a chat with the
    thread key parented to another agent is not a match. A new chat is parented to the agent, shares
    its Instructions, and is bound to the skills and objects of the agent's current chat (an agent
    with no chat contributes itself), plus the new chat. Called by the EDGE gateway, which lives
    outside this package.
```

```mdl
op listAgents
  key: org.dxos.operation.agent.list
  desc: Lists every Agent in the space with the number of chats parented to it.
  input: {}
  output: { agents: { agent: Ref<Agent>, name?: string, chats: number }[] }
  effects: [echo:read]
  requires: [Database.Service]
  note: Lists all `Agent` objects, not only ones this plugin created.
```

Memory operations (the Interview skill's tools).

```mdl
op resolveEntity
  key: org.dxos.operation.agent.resolveEntity
  desc: Finds the Person or Organization matching the handles or name, creating it if absent.
  input:
    name?: string
    handles?: { label?: string, value: string }[]   # e.g. { label: 'discord', value: '<user id>' }
    kind?: person | organization                    # default person
  output: { entity: Ref<Obj>, created: boolean }
  errors:
    AgentOperationError: neither a name nor a handle was given
  effects: [echo:read, echo:write]
  requires: [Database.Service]
  note: |
    Person: a handle match wins (value equal, and label equal when the handle has one); otherwise a
    case-insensitive match on fullName or preferredName. Handles the match lacks are appended to its
    `identities`. Organization: case-insensitive name match only; handles are ignored.
```

```mdl
op recordMemory
  key: org.dxos.operation.agent.recordMemory
  desc: Records one atomic third-person claim about the given subjects.
  input:
    content: string
    kind: fact | preference | goal | commitment | relationship | event
    origin?: stated | inferred
    subjects: Ref<Obj>[]            # at least one
    confidence?: number             # 0..1
    source?: Ref<Obj>
    supersedes?: Ref<Memory>
  output: { memory: Ref<Memory> }
  errors:
    AgentOperationError: no subjects, or confidence outside 0..1
  effects: [echo:write]
  requires: [Database.Service]
  note: One `HasSubject` per subject; a superseded memory's status becomes `superseded`.
```

```mdl
op retrieveMemories
  key: org.dxos.operation.agent.retrieveMemories
  desc: Returns the active memories about a subject (newest first) and the live goals it owns.
  input:
    subject?: Ref<Obj>              # all memories and goals if omitted
    query?: string                  # case-insensitive substring of content
    limit?: number
  output: |
    { memories: { memory: Ref<Memory>, content, kind, origin, observedAt }[],
      goals: { goal: Ref<Goal>, title, horizon, status }[] }
  effects: [echo:read]
  requires: [Database.Service]
  note: Live goals are every status but `dropped`; ties in observedAt break on id.
```

```mdl
op suggestGoal
  key: org.dxos.operation.agent.suggestGoal
  desc: Records a goal the owners described; it stays proposed until confirmed.
  input:
    title: string
    description?: string
    horizon: now | quarter | year | long-term
    owners: Ref<Obj>[]              # at least one; each a Person or Organization
    parent?: Ref<Goal>
  output: { goal: Ref<Goal> }
  errors:
    AgentOperationError: no owners, or an owner that is not a Person or Organization
  effects: [echo:write]
  requires: [Database.Service]
```

```mdl
op setGoalStatus
  key: org.dxos.operation.agent.setGoalStatus
  desc: Sets the status of a goal its owner has answered for.
  input:
    goal: Ref<Goal>
    status?: confirmed | active | achieved | dropped   # default confirmed
  output: { goal: Ref<Goal> }
  effects: [echo:write]
  requires: [Database.Service]
  note: No transition rules are enforced; any listed status may be set from any other.
```

```mdl
op updateProfile
  key: org.dxos.operation.agent.updateProfile
  desc: Rewrites the subject's profile document from its live goals and active memories.
  input:
    subject: Ref<Obj>               # Person or Organization
  output: { document: Ref<Obj> }
  effects: [echo:read, echo:write]
  requires: [Database.Service]
  note: |
    Updates the existing `ProfileOf` document's text in place (and its `lastResearchedAt`);
    otherwise creates a `Markdown.Document` parented to the subject plus a `ProfileOf` relation.
```

Discord bot operations (`DiscordOperationHandlerSet`, browser and tauri only — they call EDGE as the
user through `EdgeHttpClientService`). Every verb addresses `/compute/discord/bots/<applicationId>`.

```mdl
op startDiscordBot
  key: org.dxos.operation.agent.startDiscordBot
  desc: Starts, or reconfigures, the EDGE gateway for the binding's bot.
  input:
    binding: Ref<DiscordBinding>
  output: { status: BotStatus }
  errors:
    AgentOperationError: binding has no applicationId; EDGE unreachable; response is not a BotStatus
  effects: [http]
  requires: [Database.Service, EdgeHttpClientService]
  note: PUT with body `{ spaceId, binding: 'echo://<spaceId>/<bindingId>' }`; EDGE reads the rest from the binding.
```

```mdl
op stopDiscordBot
  key: org.dxos.operation.agent.stopDiscordBot
  desc: Stops the EDGE gateway for the binding's bot; EDGE keeps its config and thread map.
  input:
    binding: Ref<DiscordBinding>
  output: {}
  errors:
    AgentOperationError: as startDiscordBot
  effects: [http]
  requires: [Database.Service, EdgeHttpClientService]
  note: DELETE.
```

```mdl
op getDiscordBotStatus
  key: org.dxos.operation.agent.getDiscordBotStatus
  desc: Reports the EDGE gateway status of the binding's bot.
  input:
    binding: Ref<DiscordBinding>
  output: { status: BotStatus }
  errors:
    AgentOperationError: as startDiscordBot
  effects: [http]
  requires: [Database.Service, EdgeHttpClientService]
  note: GET.
```

## Skills

```mdl
skill ConversationSkill
  key: org.dxos.skill.agentConversation
  desc: Bound to every autonomous agent's first chat; the conversational role.
  contributes:
    - op:createAgent
    - op:ensureThreadChat
    - op:listAgents
  instructions: >
    Authored in `src/skills/ConversationSkill.ts`: reply in the conversation (which may mirror a
    Discord thread), address the latest message, be concise.
```

```mdl
skill InterviewSkill
  key: org.dxos.skill.interview
  desc: Interviews a person to learn their role, goals, team and preferences, and records it.
  contributes:
    - op:resolveEntity
    - op:recordMemory
    - op:retrieveMemories
    - op:suggestGoal
    - op:setGoalStatus
    - op:updateProfile
  instructions: >
    Authored in `src/skills/InterviewSkill.ts`. Start: state the purpose, resolve the person (name and
    handles), recall what is known and do not re-ask it, and — only if a checklist tool is available —
    track four topics (role, goals, team, preferences). During: one open question at a time, reflect
    back, probe each goal (why, by when, obstacles, who), remember one claim per call with stated or
    inferred origin, supersede contradictions, propose each goal. End: read the goals back, set each
    answer's status (dropped for rejections), update the person's and any team's profile, summarise.
```

Both are contributed as `SkillDefinition`s; createAgent puts the Interview skill in every new agent's
Instructions.

## App graph

```mdl
node AgentsSection
  desc: |
    A type section for `Agent` under the space's AI group (`root/<spaceId>/ai/org.dxos.type.agent`),
    contributed here because plugin-assistant renders Agent articles but lists no section. One child
    node per Agent in the space (URL key `agent`); the section header's + ("Add agent") invokes
    op:createAgent with name '', so the new agent shows the placeholder "New agent".
  source: node:SpaceRoot
  subject: type:Agent
  actions: [op:createAgent]
```

## Components

```mdl
component DiscordBindingForm
  desc: Schema form over DiscordBinding.Properties; the token field is a picker over AccessTokens in `db`.
  props:
    db?: Database
    label?: string
    description?: string
    values?: Partial<DiscordBinding.Properties>
    autoSave?: boolean              # true once a binding exists: save on blur, no Save button
  emits:
    onSave(values: DiscordBinding.Properties)
```

```mdl
component DiscordBotStatus
  desc: |
    A banner for the gateway state. With `error` (EDGE unreachable or a bad response): error valence,
    title "Could not reach EDGE", the message as body. With no status yet: "Checking bot status".
    Otherwise the gateway label (Stopped | Connecting | Connected | Disconnected | Failed), the thread
    count ("No threads" / "N threads"), and `lastError` as a second body line, in which case the
    valence is warning regardless of the gateway state.
  props:
    status?: BotStatus
    error?: string
```

```mdl
component ProfileGraph
  desc: |
    Two labelled regions, "Goals" (title; horizon · status) and "Memories" (content; kind · origin ·
    date), or "Nothing recorded yet." when both are empty.
  props:
    goals: Goal[]
    memories: Memory[]
```

```mdl
component AgentActivity
  desc: |
    Pure activity panel (components/AgentActivity), a composite of four parts. Root: Panel with an
    ActionToolbar ("Discord bot") — Start bot (Restart bot while running), Stop bot (disabled unless
    running) and Refresh status, all disabled while a call is in flight or before a binding exists —
    over a scrolling body; enabled only while the host plank has attention, or always when no
    attendableId is given (storybook). Discord: DiscordBindingForm (Save button until a binding
    exists, auto-save after) and, once bound, DiscordBotStatus. Conversations: a "Conversations"
    list, or "No Discord threads yet." when empty. Conversation: one row (Discord icon, thread
    title or "Untitled thread", compact last-activity Timestamp) that emits onSelect.
  props:
    attendableId?: string
    bound?: boolean
    running?: boolean
    busy?: boolean
    values?: Partial<DiscordBinding.Properties>
    status?: BotStatus
    error?: string
    conversations: { id: string, title?: string, lastActivity?: string }[]
  emits:
    onStart()
    onStop()
    onRefresh()
    onSave(values: DiscordBinding.Properties)
    onSelect(id: string)
```

```mdl
component AgentActivityContainer
  desc: |
    Container (containers/AgentActivity) wiring AgentActivity to the agent. Finds the agent's
    DiscordBinding and its Chats with child-of queries (`Filter.and(Filter.type(T), Filter.childOf(agent))`,
    never `.children()` — EDGE cannot run traversals). With no binding, saving adds one parented to the
    agent (`db.add`, no operation); with one, edits auto-save into it. Lists the chats carrying a
    `discord.com` meta key (bridged threads), newest first by id; each row subscribes to its own chat
    name and feed so last activity is the newest message's `created`. Selecting a row opens the chat.
    Status is fetched on mount and polled every 5s while a binding exists; a failed poll keeps the last
    status beside the error.
  props:
    agent: Agent
    attendableId?: string
  state:
    status?: BotStatus
    error?: string
    busy: boolean
  actions:
    start() → op:startDiscordBot
    stop() → op:stopDiscordBot, then op:getDiscordBotStatus
    refresh() → op:getDiscordBotStatus
    select(chat) → org.dxos.operation.appToolkit.open
```

```mdl
component ProfileProperties
  desc: |
    ProfileGraph over the subject's live goals (owner refers to the subject; not dropped) and active
    memories (HasSubject targets the subject), newest first. Subscribes to every Memory and Goal atom
    so status changes (confirmed, superseded) re-render without a membership change.
  props:
    subject: Person | Organization
```

## Surfaces

```mdl
companion AgentActivity
  of: type:Agent
